gcm/live-draw: fragment WPOS honours the shader window's origin (LD_WPOS_ORIGIN=0 old).

Symptom (Killzone 2, Corinth River): a vertically mirrored, translucent copy of the frame shows over parts of the
picture (an upside-down Garza head below Garza at the railing, girders across the walls and windows).

Cause: NV4097_SET_SHADER_WINDOW (0x1D88; height bits 0-11, origin bits 12-15: 0 top, 1 bottom, pixel centre bits
16-19). With the origin at the bottom the RSX gives the fragment program WPOS.y = height - y (RPCS3: wpos_scale -1,
wpos_bias height). The decompiler always returned SV_Position (y from the top), so a program on a bottom-origin
window that addresses a screen-space texture from WPOS read it upside down.

Fix: a program that reads WPOS (rsx_fp_reads_wpos) on a bottom-origin window reads input.position as
float4(p.x, height - p.y, p.zw), applied before patch 2088's per-pixel centre. The height is in the pipeline key only
for those programs, so other pipelines keep their keys. [wpos-origin] logs the first 64 distinct (window, target)
pairs of WPOS-reading draws and a count every 65536 such draws. ASSUMPTION: the pixel-centre field is still ignored.
Behaviour follows RPCS3 (GPL-2.0), wpos_scale / wpos_bias in its fragment-program decompiler; read, not copied.
Written for this port.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c b/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
--- a/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
@@ -637,6 +637,26 @@ u32 rsx_fp_texture_bx2_units(const u8* ucode, u32 max_bytes)
     return 0;
 }
 
+/* KZ2 patch 2090: does any instruction read WPOS (input register 0)? The same walk as the unit scans above. */
+int rsx_fp_reads_wpos(const u8* ucode, u32 max_bytes)
+{
+    if (!ucode) return 0;
+    for (u32 off = 0; off + 16 <= max_bytes;) {
+        const u32 w0 = rsx_fp_read_word(ucode + off);
+        const u32 w1 = rsx_fp_read_word(ucode + off + 4);
+        const u32 w2 = rsx_fp_read_word(ucode + off + 8);
+        const u32 w3 = rsx_fp_read_word(ucode + off + 12);
+        const u32 src = (w0 & FP_INPUT_SRC_MASK) >> FP_INPUT_SRC_SHIFT;
+        if (!(w2 & FP_BRANCH) && src == 0 &&
+            ((w1 & 3u) == FP_REG_TYPE_INPUT || (w2 & 3u) == FP_REG_TYPE_INPUT || (w3 & 3u) == FP_REG_TYPE_INPUT))
+            return 1;
+        off += 16;
+        if (!(w2 & FP_BRANCH) && ((w1 & 3u) == 2 || (w2 & 3u) == 2 || (w3 & 3u) == 2)) off += 16;
+        if (w0 & FP_END) return 0;
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
